  "worked_solution": "First, using the laws of logarithms, we observe that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2-x) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2(1-\\frac{x}{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20612+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1-\\frac{x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Maclaurin series for $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1+x)=x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-\\frac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1-\\frac{x}{2}) & =(-\\frac{x}{2})-\\frac{1}{2}{(-\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{(-\\frac{x}{2})}^{3}-\u22ef \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})+\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{8})-\u22ef \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{24}-\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the desired result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2-x) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20612+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1-\\frac{x}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20612+(-\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{24}-\u22ef) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20612-\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
